{
 "base_commit": "7e457e85",
 "method": "The suite file of an exported copy of each commit was given a wrapper around the keeper module's keep function (the one every keeper calls), and nothing else. For each row it counts the calls of the keep step, the calls that answered ok, the calls asked for a snapshot, the numbered snapshot folders with a manifest that appeared in the store during a call, and the kept refs under refs/veldo/kept/ that appeared in the main repository during a call. A kill inside the keep step is counted too. The worktree of this ticket was not changed for it.",
 "now_commit": "e31646da (the suite and every module are the same at 1f8aaebb)",
 "reading": "All 31 rows are green on both. Each of the 19 rows that were red at f347196e makes the same number of keep step calls as on the base, the same number answer ok and the same number of snapshots is written. 13 of the 19 call the keep step; the other 6 never did (ac4/store-protected reads the snapshot ac4/outside-git made, ac6/three-deferrals, signal/removing-while-the-remover-runs, keep/ledger-reads-itself, keep/names, keep/canon). Where the item became a worker clone more kept refs are written, never fewer: a clone keeps every ref it has.",
